<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Why South Africa's local elections matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb43facfaba523f792e37bd15ea65dabe7faba1e4bd1b6688f94d0bf241c9391</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-south-africa-s-local-elections-matter/a-79842695--3bc8ee9505ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-south-africa-s-local-elections-matter/a-79842695?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Africans head to the polls on Wednesday amid water shortages, frustration with local services and questions over whether the ANC's support will keep falling.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war: Merz doubts Russia is serious about a truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ead3702e38e1c55af2b80d90c2c64b8c08f14fe273e3f8ac3eb549f3c716eeeb</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-war-merz-doubts-russia-is-serious-about-a-truce/a-79836026--11d120b4fdbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-war-merz-doubts-russia-is-serious-about-a-truce/a-79836026?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz met with Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Berlin, and emphasized Europe needs to be included in any peace talks with Russia. At the same time, Merz doubts Moscow is serious about wanting a truce.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What's behind new India-China border tensions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b251bb419c43d2d75c9c913ceb5c65dc578941339e74d8e329fe1bed08b75a4</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-behind-new-india-china-border-tensions/a-79843273--1eb1b5b74626.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-behind-new-india-china-border-tensions/a-79843273?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities have confirmed a new border "face-off" between Indian and Chinese troops in Arunachal Pradesh, raising questions about the still fragile thaw in relations between New Delhi and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c6eda95742313984642b3470783f5577c3f7fd89e83a7fa9b0055c7eba2e81d</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Cyprus: From ties with Russia to a strategic alignment with the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c973cab1d5c5baa8bbdfa549a198f95d9f31a0dd9491c427d53feaf2576ad401</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251--5a66c266e064.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Republic of Cyprus long balanced ties between Russia and the West. Now, it is phasing out Russian weapons, expanding defense cooperation with the United States and redefining its place in the Eastern Mediterranean.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What US midterm elections mean for Ukraine, Iran and elsewhere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:247c4de981635a1670ef930de1ce82321eb20ff65ae755935f2bc849c1132b7a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423--c94a74658887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans control the US Congress, but that could change after the midterm elections. The outcome of the ballot will not only impact domestic policy but also conflicts in Europe and the Middle East.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi clashes near Taiz leave residents in a 'state of panic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2635f4bc98f1717f06d8fd61501858acd3af9bf473df9f0e09c77ee2482e6b71</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthi-clashes-near-taiz-leave-residents-in-a-state-of-panic/a-79836913--fbc4d150c8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthi-clashes-near-taiz-leave-residents-in-a-state-of-panic/a-79836913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Yemeni government forces has intensified around the city of Taiz. Residents face growing shortages of food, water and medical supplies as thousands flee their homes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights to European airports targeted by bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8994ab4d2bafc7545894f20621282f0e0b4899509572b3086d5fb8fe11ce83ae</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434--863c4364baea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bomb threats involved two passenger planes bound for Warsaw, a Ryanair flight from London to Spain, and a fourth flight traveling from Israel to the Bulgarian capital, Sofia. No explosives were found.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can US midterm election really change Trump's Iran policy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:580c4ac62433bf377748c8bad234517b23b62d90c89dc23d95f2fc35f4752576</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-us-midterm-election-really-change-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79840683--41923630eaef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-us-midterm-election-really-change-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79840683?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US midterms are at hand, but their impact on the Iran war remains far from clear. Analysts say the Washington political elite may not be as divided on Iran as it appears.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Spanish player dies on after cardiac arrest on the pitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77d84fdf814d6594d15de2d819f762b405191c2efa08129b4e81803927979165</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398--59e3eb0d85d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tenerife forward Jesus de Miguel has died following a collision with the opposing goalkeeper. The Spanish second division club has said it is "heartbroken" at the loss.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Asian Cup postponed due to Middle East conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5daf886f35f04bb2d6cdf823a1a734999fa2abbaf6dd95e13af599b34b9230c4</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334--1d2a8af2e01e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Cup has become the latest sporting event to be affected by the ongoing conflict in the Middle East. Organizers cite "exceptional circumstances" in Saudi Arabia, which has seen several Houthi attacks of late.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could the AI boom make borrowing more expensive in Europe?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:876f2b4d7351d803fc0de04bd0b3121fd9076c75a2ebfcba047c624ff06c1a86</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985--c654959bd451.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France, Germany and Italy face a volatile bond market as war inflation bites. With US tech giants now issuing billions in AI bonds, they are competing with cash-strapped European governments.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Americans vote in elections seen as referendum on Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3228e31850da41742b7410b9d98df69d1a378bc8b79f03649e997d68a97a272</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-americans-vote-in-elections-seen-as-referendum-on-trump/live-79829440--222b36fa2df5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-americans-vote-in-elections-seen-as-referendum-on-trump/live-79829440?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The crucial midterms will determine how much power President Donald Trump has to make changes in the last two years of his term. Follow DW's live updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US midterm election: How it works, why it's important and races to watch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbbd5a97c13ba3eb44728408f02dafaf9740bd2135d565b83f6747e7a6104ef</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-midterm-election-how-it-works-why-it-s-important-and-races-to-watch/a-79789932--11a06f87bac3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterm-election-how-it-works-why-it-s-important-and-races-to-watch/a-79789932?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US voters are electing a new Congress. The results will be decisive for the future of the United States, and a judgment on Donald Trump's second term as president.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Ukraine in focus at Berlin Security Conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f565e4305a1f6124560100699233722833c284f1712a2b244c6c285721e83985</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T07:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ukraine-in-focus-at-berlin-security-conference/live-79835322--417ad1cade50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ukraine-in-focus-at-berlin-security-conference/live-79835322?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A security conference in the German capital is to examine ways of defending against threats from Russia. The justice minister has put forward a bill that would raise penalties for sexual offenses. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cyclone Murasu wreaks havoc after landfall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1add93d3f007b431f9235223c9ce7bd79f62fc6376dafa4c6c14671ef3c0c70</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-murasu-wreaks-havoc-after-landfall/live-79835410--5b6874a56b13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-murasu-wreaks-havoc-after-landfall/live-79835410?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cyclone Murasu made landfall in Andhra Pradesh, leaving a trail of destruction. Weather agencies have warned of heavy rainfall in the next 12 hours. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea denies role in record Binance hack, calls US charge 'provocation'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5ac1a701c791104df85bdff60a4680ab891c670fbea6e4e52773c8d4b85f6cd</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T05:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-denies-role-in-record-binance-hack-calls-us-charge-provocation/a-79835321--e1cb1eacace4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-denies-role-in-record-binance-hack-calls-us-charge-provocation/a-79835321?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kim Yo Jong dismissed FBI claims that North Korean hackers stole more than $6 billion from Binance, as the exchange began reopening withdrawals on more networks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: Trump labels Democrats 'dangerous' ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4cdd3e4920e41eafa6693b62167c39a1cc79a7993e286dc5d657859a380e2b4f</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T23:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-trump-labels-democrats-dangerous-ahead-of-midterms/a-79834945--a5b301b7e339.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-trump-labels-democrats-dangerous-ahead-of-midterms/a-79834945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said the Democrats nominated "the most extreme and dangerous" candidates in US history in the midterms. He also lowered expectations by saying a sitting president "doesn't win" the midterms.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to block 20,000 California ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68b5657f741e60fbd4b47994d82431602ba5ee4394bcb3198cd0ad413a3e8e18</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T23:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-block-20-000-california-ballots/a-79833739--5ec8b96f0332.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-block-20-000-california-ballots/a-79833739?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration had appealed to the Supreme Court over claims that a list of more than 20,000 ballots in California include non-US citizens.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: At least 26 killed in Russian strikes on aid center</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9da686321f945716172d2e2c5c0697aa9110cf99135ff13b27e60bd92d2e45e</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T21:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-at-least-26-killed-in-russian-strikes-on-aid-center/live-79825079--7b2f891543f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-at-least-26-killed-in-russian-strikes-on-aid-center/live-79825079?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 26 people were killed in Russian airstrikes on a school that was serving as an aid distribution center in Zaporizhzhia, a southern Ukrainian region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US to drop South Africa, Rwanda from duty-free trade initiative</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8824c6cbe574abbf3659b4cc9941d4545645d2203827a5d71da1f416a1e956ba</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T21:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-to-drop-south-africa-rwanda-from-duty-free-trade-initiative/a-79834508--6eef768d2e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-to-drop-south-africa-rwanda-from-duty-free-trade-initiative/a-79834508?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has said South Africa and Rwanda are breaking the rules of the AGOA free trade initiative, a centerpiece of US economic engagement with sub-Saharan Africa.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
